WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.263
Guess what. Uncle
Crowley? I'm hungry.

2
00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.392
<i>So. Amara's growing
like a radioactive weed?</i>

3
00:00:07.541 --> 00:00:08.952
<i>By stuffing her face with souls.</i>

4
00:00:08.976 --> 00:00:11.616
If she's half as powerful as I
think she is. I want her on my team.

5
00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.306
The Darkness is
almost infinite power.

6
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.860
<i>We're bound. Dean.</i>

7
00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:16.980
God kicked this
thing's ass once before.

8
00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:18.846
We need your help. God.

9
00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.548
You know who we need
to help with The Darkness.

10
00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.690
Hello. Demon Tablet!

11
00:00:23.924 --> 00:00:26.655
He was God's scribe. He
did hear about everything.

12
00:00:26.927 --> 00:00:29.226
Detective Madsen? I saw a
guy hanging around earlier.

13
00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.420
That's Len.

14
00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:31.908
<i>I think Amara
sucked out his soul.</i>

15
00:00:31.932 --> 00:00:33.612
I'll confess to all the
murders. Holy crap.

16
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.700
That way I can't get out.

17
00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:36.579
We can't kill him 'cause
he hasn't done anything yet.

18
00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.936
We don't wanna kill him.
We wanna save people.

19
00:00:39.306 --> 00:00:40.906
Right. your new rules.

20
00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.265
What can I do to help?

21
00:00:42.476 --> 00:00:44.153
No. no. You just. uh.
sit there. take a breather.

22
00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.440
- Watch some Netflix.
- Okay.

23
00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:47.386
<i>Besides. we got
bigger fish to fry.</i>

24
00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.973
Bye. Dean. I'll see you soon.

25
00:00:56.023 --> 00:00:58.334
So. she says dating's gonna
break my focus for academics.

26
00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.198
but that I'm allowed to
date over summer break.

27
00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:01.820
How does that work?

28
00:01:02.229 --> 00:01:04.698
Like. "Hi. I'm Goldie. I'm
only romantically available

29
00:01:04.865 --> 00:01:06.857
"from June to August.
but wanna go steady?"

30
00:01:09.136 --> 00:01:10.866
I hate her. Like. look at me.

31
00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.370
I have to hang out by the
tracks just to get my snack on.

32
00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:16.002
- She won't let you eat chips?
- Well. she'll let me.

33
00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.835
But just so she can make
this face the whole time.

34
00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:24.913
It's like. "Sorry. Mom. I can't
survive on menthol and diet soda

35
00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.177
"like you can."

36
00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:27.420
Mmm.

37
00:01:28.589 --> 00:01:29.682
What? No.

38
00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:34.461
Look. I hate my parents. too. Goldie.
They suck. But I got a curfew. Bye.

39
00:01:35.162 --> 00:01:37.097
Fine. Bye.

40
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.500
Whoa.

41
00:01:42.069 --> 00:01:43.230
Hey.

42
00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:45.496
Where are your parents?

43
00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.409
I don't have any parents.

44
00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.570
I'm sorry. Um...

45
00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.207
Are you okay? Do
you want something?

46
00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.714
I want to be like you.

47
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:10.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

48
00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.152
Midnight snack?

49
00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.523
Don't think I don't know
what you've been up to.

50
00:02:42.062 --> 00:02:45.055
You can try to deny it.
but the evidence is. well...

51
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.101
You told me to stop
feeding on your demons.

52
00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:52.438
Well... I stopped
feeding on demons.

53
00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.698
I thought I was clear.

54
00:02:53.874 --> 00:02:57.709
Going out there? Where
they can see you? It's too risky.

55
00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.738
I'm a growing
girl. I need to eat.

56
00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:05.947
Actions have consequences
around here. Amara.

57
00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.752
You've had the run of the Court.

58
00:03:07.988 --> 00:03:09.422
We've seen what
you've made of it.

59
00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:15.624
Believe me. this is going to hurt
me way more than it hurts you.

60
00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:17.891
I'm sorry. my dear.

61
00:03:19.099 --> 00:03:20.192
You're grounded.

62
00:03:27.074 --> 00:03:28.440
You're strong...

63
00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:32.635
But you need to
remember I'm stronger.

64
00:03:34.448 --> 00:03:35.711
For now.

65
00:03:54.101 --> 00:03:55.878
You said you had a good
feeling about that one.

66
00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.702
Yeah. well. it seemed
like a solid lead. Dean.

67
00:03:57.838 --> 00:04:00.330
Only a soulless psycho
would kill the family cat.

68
00:04:00.507 --> 00:04:02.987
Yeah. unless the family cat
decides to take a nap in the dryer.

69
00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.744
You know. we've been here since Monday and
still haven't found another legit victim.

70
00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.074
Maybe Amara moved on or
stopped feeding altogether.

71
00:04:09.883 --> 00:04:13.684
Well. finding her victims is still
the best shot we got at finding her.

72
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.979
Not actually true.

73
00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:21.098
Oh. What. you think he's ready?
He's had a pretty rough go of it lately.

74
00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.524
Which one of us hasn't?

75
00:04:23.697 --> 00:04:27.327
It seems insane to leave our one
and only angel friend on the bench.

76
00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:31.367
- I'll call him.
- Thank you.

77
00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.818
<i>We did this time. but it
literally doesn't matter.</i>

78
00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.421
<i>Well. we're gonna get to all
the results in just a second.</i>

79
00:04:38.445 --> 00:04:39.856
<i>We're gonna start with.</i>

80
00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.576
<i>let's go back
to our first story.</i>

81
00:04:42.349 --> 00:04:44.215
<i>Louis. Scilla and Edwin.</i>

82
00:04:44.451 --> 00:04:46.477
- Hi.
- Cas. how you doing. buddy?

83
00:04:48.722 --> 00:04:49.985
I'm fine.

84
00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.724
Find anything on Metatron?

85
00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.794
Nothing on angel radio.

86
00:04:56.263 --> 00:04:58.103
How long has it been
since you left the bunker?

87
00:04:58.165 --> 00:05:00.645
Well. why would I leave? I've
got everything I need right here.

88
00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.034
<i>Wait. is th...</i>

89
00:05:02.903 --> 00:05:05.372
- Are you watching <i>Jenny Jones?</i>
<i>- It's a rerun.</i>

90
00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.736
She's just about to
announce the paternity results.

91
00:05:08.942 --> 00:05:11.223
<i>You are the father.</i>

92
00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.704
<i>Jenny. he is not
ready to be a father.</i>

93
00:05:14.915 --> 00:05:18.215
Okay. I thought you were going with
socially acceptable binge-watching.

94
00:05:18.485 --> 00:05:20.647
You know. <i>The Wire.
Game of Thrones.</i>

95
00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:24.352
Yeah. well. man can't
live on caviar alone. Dean.

96
00:05:25.926 --> 00:05:28.521
Well. you sound
weird. okay? Bad weird.

97
00:05:28.962 --> 00:05:31.602
- Now. I have been down this road before...
- What's up. Detective?

98
00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:33.564
I have heard the siren
song from the idiot box.

99
00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:35.378
and I'm telling you.
whatever you're looking for.

100
00:05:35.402 --> 00:05:36.563
<i>you won't find it in there.</i>

101
00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.499
<i>So. do me a favor.</i>

102
00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:41.037
Turn off the TV. go
outside and get some air.

103
00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:44.388
We're in the dark here. pal. I
need you back in the game. okay?

104
00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:46.174
Yeah. I...

105
00:05:47.147 --> 00:05:48.147
I got it.

106
00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.915
Yeah. well. thanks for letting me
know. We'll head out there right now.

107
00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.786
- You got it.
- What's up?

108
00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:55.516
<i>That was Detective Madsen.</i>

109
00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:58.051
Remember our friend Len?

110
00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:01.159
Uh. Weird as hell. soulless.
took-the-rap-for-all-the-murders Len?

111
00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.955
Yeah. He's dead.

112
00:06:28.188 --> 00:06:29.554
<i>Cass? Cass!</i>

113
00:06:30.257 --> 00:06:31.281
<i>Don't do this.</i>

114
00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:36.758
<i>Okay. this isn't you. it's
the spell. You can beat this!</i>

115
00:06:39.299 --> 00:06:41.291
<i>I will end you!</i>

116
00:06:41.735 --> 00:06:42.794
No!

117
00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:45.828
<i>Don't!</i>

118
00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:52.016
<i>I won't let you walk
out of this room.</i>

119
00:07:04.224 --> 00:07:05.590
Marco got one
of them last night.

120
00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:07.151
A Len Fleischer.

121
00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:09.218
Tell Marco to keep looking.

122
00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:12.057
The last thing I need is one
of Amara's candy wrappers

123
00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:17.029
blabbing to angels or hunters
about what. who. happened to them.

124
00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:21.632
Where is everyone?

125
00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:24.076
Oh. Our ranks have
been a bit thin. since...

126
00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:26.276
Amara ate everybody.

127
00:07:27.147 --> 00:07:29.507
I've got some fresh numbers
for you to go over before Court.

128
00:07:29.716 --> 00:07:31.184
Soul projections.
they're not good.

129
00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:33.291
We're down for the
quarter. which means that...

130
00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.788
That door was supposed to
be locked and guarded 24/7.

131
00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.014
Of course. sir.

132
00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:40.522
I don't see a guard.

133
00:07:40.794 --> 00:07:42.194
Uh. Right.

134
00:07:42.429 --> 00:07:45.991
Must be a mix-up. We're
short-staffed and all. so...

135
00:07:46.366 --> 00:07:52.067
Congratulations. You've been demoted.
No one goes in or out of that room.

136
00:08:00.814 --> 00:08:03.545
Thought maybe a relative
of one of Len's victims.

137
00:08:04.551 --> 00:08:06.679
But it doesn't feel
like a revenge killing.

138
00:08:08.021 --> 00:08:09.080
Too clean.

139
00:08:09.656 --> 00:08:11.090
Like an assassination.

140
00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:13.738
<i>- Detective?</i>
- Excuse me.

141
00:08:15.028 --> 00:08:16.257
- You smell that?
- Yeah.

142
00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.736
Yeah. either the detective
needs to change his diet or...

143
00:08:18.898 --> 00:08:20.833
Sulfur. Len was
killed by a demon.

144
00:08:21.101 --> 00:08:23.502
Yeah. but why would a demon
run a hit on a guy with no soul?

145
00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.350
That's like a Cracker
Jack without a prize.

146
00:08:25.438 --> 00:08:26.906
Hands off. Deputy Doody!

147
00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:36.309
- Who's the girl?
- Goldie Schmidtlapp.

148
00:08:37.017 --> 00:08:40.545
Was a normal kid. snapped this morning.
tried to kill her mom with a frying pan.

149
00:08:41.921 --> 00:08:43.981
First the ax murders.
then Len. now this?

150
00:08:44.157 --> 00:08:45.597
We're gonna need
to talk to the kid.

151
00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:48.855
<i>That's four legs on four wheels.</i>

152
00:08:51.865 --> 00:08:54.528
<i>Aw. That dog thinks it's people.</i>

153
00:08:56.503 --> 00:08:59.837
<i>Up next. a very upsetting
story out of Omaha.</i>

154
00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.542
<i>A downtown bar fight
escalated tragically last night.</i>

155
00:09:03.977 --> 00:09:09.109
<i>and OWW-Two News brings
you an exclusive video of the event.</i>

156
00:09:09.783 --> 00:09:12.719
<i>The footage you are about
to view is extremely graphic.</i>

157
00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:28.865
<i>Efforts were made to
resuscitate the victim but...</i>

158
00:09:54.561 --> 00:09:56.801
<i>Hey. Officer? Still haven't
gotten my phone call.</i>

159
00:09:57.063 --> 00:09:59.063
Do you think I could get
a pizza delivered in here?

160
00:10:01.901 --> 00:10:04.029
- You're not the deputy.
- Nope.

161
00:10:10.143 --> 00:10:12.510
The boss' daughter's been
making a mess in town.

162
00:10:12.745 --> 00:10:14.145
and it's my job to clean it up.

163
00:10:15.982 --> 00:10:17.280
Nothing personal.

164
00:10:32.765 --> 00:10:34.233
Nice work. Goldie.

165
00:10:35.735 --> 00:10:37.397
So. Crowley and Amara.

166
00:10:40.507 --> 00:10:41.507
Huh.

167
00:10:48.348 --> 00:10:49.941
Rise and shine. buttercup.

168
00:10:52.185 --> 00:10:53.209
Now...

169
00:10:54.287 --> 00:10:55.721
About what you were saying...

170
00:10:56.623 --> 00:10:58.387
What's Crowley doing with Amara?

171
00:10:59.759 --> 00:11:03.059
Don't know. Don't care.
Wouldn't tell you if I did.

172
00:11:05.098 --> 00:11:07.567
Well. we already know
she's growing up fast.

173
00:11:08.268 --> 00:11:10.965
Yeah. well. demon souls.
They do a body good.

174
00:11:16.409 --> 00:11:18.275
The little moppet tore
through half my buds

175
00:11:18.444 --> 00:11:20.106
before Crowley
put her on a diet.

176
00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:22.542
She didn't like that.

177
00:11:23.483 --> 00:11:26.043
Started sneaking out to get
her fill. You know how kids are.

178
00:11:26.819 --> 00:11:28.219
But Daddy put his foot down.

179
00:11:30.857 --> 00:11:32.723
- Where's he hiding her?
- Oh.

180
00:11:33.359 --> 00:11:35.760
I'm happy to keep
gossiping with you boys. but...

181
00:11:36.196 --> 00:11:38.529
You want actionable
intelligence?

182
00:11:40.033 --> 00:11:41.695
Torture me if you want.

183
00:11:43.403 --> 00:11:44.837
I know you'll just
kill me anyway.

184
00:11:46.506 --> 00:11:47.506
Hmm.

185
00:11:48.641 --> 00:11:50.405
Well. looks like a
stalemate to me.

186
00:11:51.644 --> 00:11:53.389
I guess we'll go ahead
and kill him right now.

187
00:11:53.413 --> 00:11:54.642
No. no. no. Dean. wait.

188
00:11:58.484 --> 00:12:00.077
We can exorcise him.

189
00:12:01.688 --> 00:12:03.213
- What?
- Save his meatsuit.

190
00:12:05.959 --> 00:12:07.188
My two cents?

191
00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:10.023
You exorcise me. let
me smoke on outta here?

192
00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:12.558
I give you my word
not to tell Crowley.

193
00:12:14.801 --> 00:12:17.641
Hey. you heard me. He's hardly
my favorite guy at the moment.

194
00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.571
- I...
- Wait a second. Shut up.

195
00:12:24.711 --> 00:12:26.509
Well. would you look at that?

196
00:12:30.683 --> 00:12:32.743
There's no way his
suit survived that wound.

197
00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:33.952
Mmm-mmm.

198
00:12:35.588 --> 00:12:36.920
All right.

199
00:12:38.825 --> 00:12:39.918
Crap.

200
00:12:56.542 --> 00:12:57.542
- Hey.
- Hey.

201
00:12:57.777 --> 00:13:00.144
- Where'd you ditch the body?
- School playground.

202
00:13:00.713 --> 00:13:02.375
- Come on.
- Hospital parking lot.

203
00:13:03.249 --> 00:13:05.275
- What do you got?
- Well. good news.

204
00:13:05.451 --> 00:13:07.044
I was able to hack his phone.

205
00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.820
Got the coordinates
of his call history.

206
00:13:09.055 --> 00:13:11.581
I guess Crowley must have had
him tailing Amara or something.

207
00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:13.102
'cause he was
at all three spots.

208
00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:16.290
He was at the Lizzie Borden
house. where Len got his soul taken.

209
00:13:16.462 --> 00:13:18.422
He was at the bar where
Sydney got her soul taken.

210
00:13:18.531 --> 00:13:21.433
And he was here. where Goldie
said Amara approached her.

211
00:13:22.135 --> 00:13:24.400
- Hmm. So. somewhere in there?
- Yeah. maybe.

212
00:13:24.971 --> 00:13:26.811
But what I don't get is.
why would Crowley have

213
00:13:26.973 --> 00:13:28.703
Amara on Earth
in the first place?

214
00:13:29.375 --> 00:13:31.375
I mean. wouldn't it be
smarter to keep her in Hell?

215
00:13:32.779 --> 00:13:35.739
Yeah. but then he'd have to spend
more time there. and he hates that place.

216
00:13:36.482 --> 00:13:37.482
Oh. right.

217
00:13:38.484 --> 00:13:40.724
I keep forgetting about you
and Crowley's summer of love.

218
00:13:43.022 --> 00:13:45.301
I'm not seeing much inside
this radius that he'd like better.

219
00:13:45.325 --> 00:13:47.285
- I mean. you got farms. you got swamps...
- Yeah.

220
00:13:47.393 --> 00:13:49.953
- This P.O.I.? What's that?
- Point of interest.

221
00:13:50.296 --> 00:13:51.730
I know what it... What is it?

222
00:13:52.098 --> 00:13:53.896
- Well. let's find out.
- Yeah.

223
00:14:02.775 --> 00:14:06.075
The Needham Asylum.
Decommissioned in '63.

224
00:14:07.013 --> 00:14:08.811
Sound like Crowley's
kind of place to you?

225
00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:24.991
What are you looking at?

226
00:14:26.833 --> 00:14:29.268
Still learning all you
can about the world?

227
00:14:30.737 --> 00:14:35.334
If nonsensical slogans attached to
idiotic pictures of domestic animals

228
00:14:35.508 --> 00:14:37.739
- counts as the world.
- Excuse me?

229
00:14:39.846 --> 00:14:41.007
Memes.

230
00:14:42.315 --> 00:14:43.315
Ah.

231
00:14:47.854 --> 00:14:50.756
Look. I know. to
you. my rules seem...

232
00:14:51.758 --> 00:14:53.124
Unfair. arbitrary.

233
00:14:53.593 --> 00:14:55.687
As though I'm doing
all this just to hurt you.

234
00:14:56.062 --> 00:14:57.792
I don't care why
you do anything.

235
00:14:59.699 --> 00:15:01.793
I just want you to know
that I'm not a monster.

236
00:15:05.838 --> 00:15:07.033
Jervis?

237
00:15:12.211 --> 00:15:15.181
I can't have you eating
whatever. whenever.

238
00:15:15.381 --> 00:15:16.713
however much you want.

239
00:15:18.951 --> 00:15:20.817
I thought you might
appreciate a little snack.

240
00:15:23.956 --> 00:15:25.982
I'm not hungry.

241
00:15:42.308 --> 00:15:43.936
I'll leave you to your memes.

242
00:15:56.589 --> 00:16:00.048
I have no idea
what I'm doing here.

243
00:16:01.494 --> 00:16:03.190
Not a bleeding clue.

244
00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:06.925
Moment to moment. what makes
you happy. what will set you off?

245
00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:10.092
How to even begin to
forge a connection with you.

246
00:16:10.436 --> 00:16:12.871
But what I do know is
you're growing so fast.

247
00:16:13.773 --> 00:16:15.241
And it terrifies me.

248
00:16:17.076 --> 00:16:18.169
I bet.

249
00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.608
You only want me
for the power I'll wield.

250
00:16:23.182 --> 00:16:26.118
And you know. soon enough.
I won't need you anymore.

251
00:16:27.854 --> 00:16:31.052
So. we're really
gonna do this? Now?

252
00:16:31.591 --> 00:16:32.615
Hell. yeah.

253
00:16:32.825 --> 00:16:34.536
I've been looking for a
chance to get back at Crowley

254
00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:36.400
ever since that crap he
pulled in Cedar Rapids.

255
00:16:36.429 --> 00:16:39.074
Especially now that I know he tricked
me and made off with The Darkness.

256
00:16:39.098 --> 00:16:40.218
No. that's not what I meant.

257
00:16:40.533 --> 00:16:42.593
We're going in to kill Amara.

258
00:16:43.769 --> 00:16:44.998
Are you ready for that?

259
00:16:46.672 --> 00:16:47.731
Why wouldn't I be?

260
00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:50.435
Because we don't know the
first thing about her. Dean.

261
00:16:50.977 --> 00:16:53.355
We don't know her powers. We
don't know how to take her down.

262
00:16:53.379 --> 00:16:55.424
Hell. you know what? We don't
even know if she can be killed.

263
00:16:55.448 --> 00:16:57.815
I know. But she's too
big of a threat to wait.

264
00:16:58.718 --> 00:17:01.038
I say we go in there and we
hit her with everything we got.

265
00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:13.927
You have tremendous power
and soon. you'll have even more.

266
00:17:15.434 --> 00:17:17.903
But I have something you lack.

267
00:17:20.439 --> 00:17:22.965
Wisdom. Experience.

268
00:17:25.044 --> 00:17:28.014
I helped put Lucifer
back in his cage.

269
00:17:28.981 --> 00:17:31.780
I rose through the ranks
of Hell. defeated all comers.

270
00:17:32.118 --> 00:17:33.916
to claim the throne.

271
00:17:34.587 --> 00:17:39.423
And. a few minor setbacks
aside. I'm still here.

272
00:17:41.928 --> 00:17:45.057
I don't know how to impart what
I've learned to you. how to teach you.

273
00:17:46.332 --> 00:17:47.772
And at the rate
that you're growing.

274
00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.994
I'll probably never get
the chance to figure it out.

275
00:17:52.605 --> 00:17:54.403
Perhaps you don't
need my tutelage.

276
00:17:57.043 --> 00:18:00.309
But I believe. deep
down in my gut.

277
00:18:01.747 --> 00:18:03.443
I have something to offer you.

278
00:18:04.483 --> 00:18:07.248
if you just give me the chance.

279
00:18:16.929 --> 00:18:18.227
What are you asking for?

280
00:18:19.732 --> 00:18:20.732
Time.

281
00:18:21.567 --> 00:18:22.591
Slow down.

282
00:18:23.269 --> 00:18:27.172
Play by my rules for
just a little bit longer.

283
00:18:29.275 --> 00:18:33.508
You give me your patience.
I'll give you my protection.

284
00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:39.410
Until you decide you
don't need it anymore.

285
00:18:47.026 --> 00:18:48.119
Okay.

286
00:18:52.031 --> 00:18:53.659
<i>Oh. This is good.</i>

287
00:18:55.868 --> 00:18:58.030
A night-leader
if ever I saw one.

288
00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:04.538
This is gonna fetch
me 500. minimum.

289
00:19:11.217 --> 00:19:12.217
I. uh...

290
00:19:12.718 --> 00:19:18.919
I know 500 sounds like
plenty. but with my overhead?

291
00:19:24.296 --> 00:19:25.559
Daddy's got to eat.

292
00:19:28.534 --> 00:19:30.503
Oh. Come on!

293
00:19:31.203 --> 00:19:33.104
Help. Please.

294
00:19:36.308 --> 00:19:39.403
I'm sorry. buddy. You
live. there's no story.

295
00:19:41.881 --> 00:19:42.881
Ugh...

296
00:19:43.516 --> 00:19:46.350
You know. there was a time...

297
00:19:47.553 --> 00:19:51.422
I could have brought you back from
the brink with a snap of my fingers.

298
00:19:53.793 --> 00:19:55.625
Not that I would have.

299
00:20:01.067 --> 00:20:02.831
But I'm not that guy anymore.

300
00:20:05.604 --> 00:20:06.833
I can't save you.

301
00:20:09.075 --> 00:20:10.270
<i>I can.</i>

302
00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.787
- How did you find me?
- Same way you found him.

303
00:20:25.257 --> 00:20:29.092
Scoured the police scanners.
got ahead of the authorities.

304
00:20:41.006 --> 00:20:42.497
What was that?

305
00:20:45.778 --> 00:20:46.905
What?

306
00:20:47.413 --> 00:20:50.076
Look. a real live
angel. caught on tape?

307
00:20:50.282 --> 00:20:53.013
That is way better than
some random homicide.

308
00:20:53.185 --> 00:20:54.619
Hey!

309
00:20:55.087 --> 00:20:57.522
Do you have any
idea how much stuff

310
00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:00.990
I had to steal and then
pawn to pay for that?

311
00:21:13.339 --> 00:21:14.739
No guards at the perimeter?

312
00:21:32.258 --> 00:21:34.489
Looks like there are no
guards at the door. either.

313
00:21:36.595 --> 00:21:38.291
You think this is
the right place. still?

314
00:21:40.199 --> 00:21:41.758
Well. warding sigils.

315
00:21:42.535 --> 00:21:43.798
And for the humans...

316
00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:47.065
Look at this. a padlock you'd
find on a middle-school locker.

317
00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:50.906
- Cocky son of a bitch.
- Dean. external security may be lax.

318
00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:53.630
but we still don't know how many
demons we're gonna face inside.

319
00:21:54.647 --> 00:21:55.945
Well. let's find out.

320
00:22:10.696 --> 00:22:12.858
Turn to the graph
at the bottom of 27

321
00:22:13.032 --> 00:22:15.968
and you'll see a nearly 40%
decrease in soul collections

322
00:22:16.135 --> 00:22:18.730
in the Pacific Northwest
over the past three years.

323
00:22:19.271 --> 00:22:21.900
An unexpected consequence
of legalized marijuana?

324
00:22:22.908 --> 00:22:24.877
<i>Some analysts think so.</i>

325
00:22:25.611 --> 00:22:28.046
<i>Others are not quite so sure...</i>

326
00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:39.750
Okay. Marv.

327
00:22:41.093 --> 00:22:44.427
You're picking pockets.
leaving a man to die...

328
00:22:45.764 --> 00:22:48.199
I don't know what I expected.
but this is disappointing.

329
00:22:48.667 --> 00:22:49.965
One to talk.

330
00:22:51.136 --> 00:22:53.435
You chose the life
of a wage slave.

331
00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:57.002
slinging Slurpees
for what? A month?

332
00:22:59.345 --> 00:23:01.405
I am in it to win it.

333
00:23:03.015 --> 00:23:05.814
I was at zero when
you took my grace.

334
00:23:06.819 --> 00:23:10.221
Hiding from angels.
not a cent to my name.

335
00:23:10.456 --> 00:23:11.947
But I found my calling.

336
00:23:12.458 --> 00:23:17.362
And I pulled myself up by my
bootstraps and started a business.

337
00:23:17.863 --> 00:23:20.628
And you know. my
story has only just begun.

338
00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:22.095
What story is that?

339
00:23:22.935 --> 00:23:26.099
You're preying like a
vulture on human tragedy.

340
00:23:26.305 --> 00:23:27.705
Oh. jeez.

341
00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:29.731
Castiel.

342
00:23:31.577 --> 00:23:33.842
What century are you in?

343
00:23:35.014 --> 00:23:36.744
Religion is dead!

344
00:23:37.216 --> 00:23:38.844
The novel? Deader.

345
00:23:39.952 --> 00:23:44.413
You think I'm ashamed for
dealing in fleeting visual sensation?

346
00:23:45.691 --> 00:23:50.356
In GIF-length glimpses of
horror. waste. and degradation?

347
00:23:50.696 --> 00:23:51.789
No!

348
00:23:53.332 --> 00:23:55.130
I just caught up with the times!

349
00:23:56.969 --> 00:24:00.963
Reality is the great
literature of our era.

350
00:24:01.206 --> 00:24:06.406
and I am out there. on the streets.
every single night. capturing it.

351
00:24:07.413 --> 00:24:10.747
- I am reality's author...
- Oh. Save your story.

352
00:24:10.983 --> 00:24:12.474
It is not what I came for.

353
00:24:16.755 --> 00:24:17.916
Oh.

354
00:24:19.425 --> 00:24:22.452
So. straight to business.

355
00:24:23.963 --> 00:24:27.195
You want the Demon Tablet?

356
00:24:30.469 --> 00:24:32.233
Well. you're not gonna get it.

357
00:24:33.539 --> 00:24:38.136
I have hidden it very carefully in a
place where you and your friends...

358
00:24:38.377 --> 00:24:41.006
You hid it under your mattress.

359
00:24:42.047 --> 00:24:45.916
The TV station gave me your
address and I checked the place out.

360
00:24:46.719 --> 00:24:48.347
You realize you have bedbugs?

361
00:24:49.888 --> 00:24:53.154
You broke into my apartment?

362
00:24:53.892 --> 00:24:56.953
What do you know
about The Darkness?

363
00:25:00.899 --> 00:25:01.992
The band?

364
00:25:03.369 --> 00:25:04.393
Okay.

365
00:25:04.970 --> 00:25:05.970
Uh...

366
00:25:06.472 --> 00:25:08.634
Sometimes. during
late-night writing sessions.

367
00:25:09.475 --> 00:25:11.876
when God was deep in his cups.

368
00:25:12.044 --> 00:25:15.947
he may have let slip
a few choice words.

369
00:25:21.553 --> 00:25:23.073
But I don't have
to tell you anything.

370
00:25:25.958 --> 00:25:27.551
Are you forgetting?

371
00:25:31.563 --> 00:25:34.931
You are human now. And I
could crush you like a bug.

372
00:25:35.934 --> 00:25:37.129
Could.

373
00:25:37.903 --> 00:25:39.098
But you won't.

374
00:25:42.341 --> 00:25:43.673
You think I didn't notice?

375
00:25:44.843 --> 00:25:46.812
You are broken. Castiel.

376
00:25:48.213 --> 00:25:50.842
You were always a
bit of a nancy. but this?

377
00:25:53.585 --> 00:25:56.384
You have gone full wuss.

378
00:25:58.357 --> 00:26:00.849
I don't know what it
was that happened.

379
00:26:01.226 --> 00:26:06.324
but whatever it was.
you are scarred deep.

380
00:26:07.466 --> 00:26:11.460
Paralyzed by trauma. by fear.

381
00:26:13.639 --> 00:26:16.040
I mean. look at you.
You can't even hit me.

382
00:26:23.682 --> 00:26:25.173
It's not fear.

383
00:26:33.492 --> 00:26:34.755
<i>Hey. idiot!</i> Ándale!

384
00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:37.024
<i>That's Spanish for
"Get your ass over here."</i>

385
00:26:40.766 --> 00:26:42.377
<i>- Do you think I've been paying your...</i>
- Sir?

386
00:26:42.401 --> 00:26:44.461
<i>Astronomical bar tabs
for the past five weeks</i>

387
00:26:44.670 --> 00:26:46.969
<i>so you can sleep past
noon with last night's skank?</i>

388
00:26:47.539 --> 00:26:48.539
<i>Well. Dean...</i>

389
00:26:54.179 --> 00:26:55.306
Is that him?

390
00:26:58.283 --> 00:27:01.219
You know what? Go.

391
00:27:02.187 --> 00:27:04.122
Take her out. I got 'em.

392
00:27:21.707 --> 00:27:23.369
I knew you'd come.

393
00:27:32.985 --> 00:27:34.613
I'm sorry. Amara.

394
00:27:35.954 --> 00:27:37.217
For what?

395
00:27:39.491 --> 00:27:41.153
What I have to do.

396
00:27:45.097 --> 00:27:46.497
<i>Hello. Dean.</i>

397
00:27:50.802 --> 00:27:52.361
My girl is growing up.

398
00:27:53.972 --> 00:27:57.033
Should have known it wouldn't be long
before the boys came sniffing around.

399
00:28:05.884 --> 00:28:07.819
What do you want
with her. Crowley?

400
00:28:09.588 --> 00:28:14.526
What do you think. you can use
her? Control her? You're an idiot.

401
00:28:15.527 --> 00:28:17.018
I'm not trying to control her.

402
00:28:20.699 --> 00:28:24.136
I'm helping her to realize
her fullest potential.

403
00:28:30.442 --> 00:28:31.967
Do you know how
disturbing it was

404
00:28:32.811 --> 00:28:35.542
to realize that I couldn't
bring myself to kill you?

405
00:28:36.682 --> 00:28:39.117
I've had tons of
chances over the years.

406
00:28:39.284 --> 00:28:41.150
Some you don't even
know about. But still...

407
00:28:41.920 --> 00:28:43.411
I made my peace with it.

408
00:28:44.189 --> 00:28:45.817
Embraced my softer side.

409
00:28:47.059 --> 00:28:52.020
Learned to accept that there was just
too much going on between you and I.

410
00:28:53.465 --> 00:28:54.465
Bromance.

411
00:28:55.667 --> 00:28:56.930
But you know what?

412
00:28:58.270 --> 00:28:59.829
I think I am gonna
kill you today.

413
00:29:00.906 --> 00:29:02.841
I feel different. somehow.

414
00:29:03.976 --> 00:29:06.775
Ready. What can I say?

415
00:29:07.746 --> 00:29:09.339
Fatherhood changes a man.

416
00:29:37.109 --> 00:29:38.372
The Darkness.

417
00:29:38.777 --> 00:29:40.006
What do you know?

418
00:29:41.246 --> 00:29:42.246
Okay.

419
00:29:43.282 --> 00:29:44.750
So I misjudged.

420
00:29:46.218 --> 00:29:48.187
You're not scared. You're mad.

421
00:29:48.620 --> 00:29:50.589
And I get it.

422
00:29:50.822 --> 00:29:54.987
I mean. it must suck.
being everyone's tool.

423
00:29:55.694 --> 00:29:57.287
Manipulated and used.

424
00:29:57.462 --> 00:30:01.263
By the angels. By your
enemies. By your fr...

425
00:30:11.877 --> 00:30:14.711
You thought if you
could get your grace back.

426
00:30:15.213 --> 00:30:17.341
it would help fix
you. But it hasn't.

427
00:30:21.520 --> 00:30:22.852
The Darkness.

428
00:30:23.522 --> 00:30:24.751
Why. Amara?

429
00:30:24.990 --> 00:30:27.289
I thought we had
an understanding.

430
00:30:27.859 --> 00:30:30.624
Yeah. Your promise
to protect me.

431
00:30:31.563 --> 00:30:34.294
And then. hours later. I'm
assaulted in my own room.

432
00:30:35.901 --> 00:30:38.370
Don't seem terribly upset by it.

433
00:30:38.670 --> 00:30:39.968
That's not the point.

434
00:30:40.706 --> 00:30:43.505
I've decided I don't
need your protection.

435
00:30:43.709 --> 00:30:46.201
And I certainly don't
need your captivity.

436
00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:49.680
I'm done.

437
00:31:10.669 --> 00:31:12.695
You trying out some
kind of no-kill policy?

438
00:31:16.074 --> 00:31:19.875
Who do you have to thank for
how angry you are? How lost?

439
00:31:26.885 --> 00:31:28.012
You're welcome.

440
00:31:42.968 --> 00:31:46.063
A hunter. You of all
people should know.

441
00:31:46.405 --> 00:31:50.103
Pacifism doesn't pay.

442
00:32:18.036 --> 00:32:20.972
Go on. Castiel. End me.

443
00:32:42.527 --> 00:32:43.654
No.

444
00:32:49.601 --> 00:32:51.797
All right. Two out of three.

445
00:32:54.806 --> 00:32:55.899
<i>Dean!</i>

446
00:33:01.179 --> 00:33:02.272
Dean!

447
00:33:24.536 --> 00:33:25.816
It's time.

448
00:33:26.004 --> 00:33:30.533
Time for you to blink your tired ass
back to your throne and lick your wounds.

449
00:33:31.042 --> 00:33:33.637
I'll spare your life
on one condition.

450
00:33:35.780 --> 00:33:39.080
Safe passage for Dean.
out of here. after I'm gone.

451
00:33:45.156 --> 00:33:46.215
Yes!

452
00:33:52.731 --> 00:33:53.790
Good.

453
00:33:54.866 --> 00:33:55.866
Now.

454
00:33:56.701 --> 00:33:59.193
Get out of my room.

455
00:34:04.142 --> 00:34:06.338
Oh. Please. Castiel.

456
00:34:08.046 --> 00:34:09.046
Help me.

457
00:34:10.549 --> 00:34:12.108
You said you were happy.

458
00:34:12.851 --> 00:34:14.479
Your bootstraps.

459
00:34:17.022 --> 00:34:18.320
I was faking it.

460
00:34:19.824 --> 00:34:21.122
I mean...

461
00:34:21.760 --> 00:34:23.854
I thought. "How
hard could it be?"

462
00:34:30.302 --> 00:34:31.463
You won't.

463
00:34:34.239 --> 00:34:35.298
You can't.

464
00:34:35.473 --> 00:34:36.964
<i>Can't take anymore.</i>

465
00:34:37.976 --> 00:34:40.673
Not a single human day.

466
00:34:41.313 --> 00:34:42.611
I mean...

467
00:34:42.948 --> 00:34:46.749
The indignities.
they just don't stop.

468
00:34:48.219 --> 00:34:49.243
<i>They...</i>

469
00:34:51.256 --> 00:34:55.284
Making my rent and
keeping my phone charged.

470
00:34:58.563 --> 00:35:00.293
Hemorrhoids.

471
00:35:01.967 --> 00:35:03.629
You were right. Metatron.

472
00:35:05.003 --> 00:35:06.835
I am sick of having
my strings pulled.

473
00:35:07.005 --> 00:35:11.033
Which is why I won't let you
manipulate me into letting you off easy.

474
00:35:11.309 --> 00:35:12.868
Oh...

475
00:35:16.114 --> 00:35:18.208
Tell me about The Darkness.

476
00:35:19.384 --> 00:35:20.511
Tell me.

477
00:35:21.186 --> 00:35:24.179
What is happening
here. between us?

478
00:35:27.092 --> 00:35:28.856
You save me. I save you.

479
00:35:34.032 --> 00:35:35.032
Why?

480
00:35:36.901 --> 00:35:39.666
You were the first thing
I saw when I was freed.

481
00:35:39.938 --> 00:35:42.635
And it had been so long.

482
00:35:45.577 --> 00:35:46.738
Maybe that's it.

483
00:35:48.013 --> 00:35:49.777
My first experience of...

484
00:35:50.548 --> 00:35:52.039
His creation.

485
00:35:54.753 --> 00:35:57.120
You can't help but
represent that for me.

486
00:35:58.490 --> 00:36:04.623
The sweet triumph and the even
sweeter folly of what He's wrought.

487
00:36:07.899 --> 00:36:09.367
There's no fighting it.

488
00:36:11.102 --> 00:36:12.502
I'm fascinated.

489
00:36:14.105 --> 00:36:15.265
<i>The truth.</i>

490
00:36:16.675 --> 00:36:19.406
It'd make the Bible-thumpers'
heads explode.

491
00:36:21.880 --> 00:36:24.076
I mean. they want
their God to be a...

492
00:36:24.683 --> 00:36:30.145
You know. a finger-snapping.
all-powerful Creator. you know?

493
00:36:31.089 --> 00:36:33.149
They want magic.

494
00:36:34.659 --> 00:36:36.218
Mary Poppins.

495
00:36:39.097 --> 00:36:40.895
But what he did?

496
00:36:44.269 --> 00:36:45.760
Creation?

497
00:36:46.371 --> 00:36:47.839
That took work.

498
00:36:50.075 --> 00:36:51.407
It took sacrifice.

499
00:36:55.013 --> 00:36:57.380
In order to create the world.

500
00:36:58.650 --> 00:37:02.348
God had to give up the
only thing he'd ever known.

501
00:37:05.857 --> 00:37:10.022
He had to betray and sacrifice

502
00:37:10.962 --> 00:37:12.396
his only kin.

503
00:37:16.034 --> 00:37:17.297
The Darkness.

504
00:37:20.939 --> 00:37:22.066
His sister.

505
00:37:27.312 --> 00:37:29.645
It's been great seeing
you again. Dean.

506
00:37:30.215 --> 00:37:31.740
But it's time for me to go.

507
00:37:33.251 --> 00:37:35.948
There's a whole world
out there for me to explore.

508
00:37:36.354 --> 00:37:38.346
And I can practically taste it.

509
00:37:41.559 --> 00:37:45.291
Soon. I'll be strong enough
to do what I came here to do.

510
00:37:46.931 --> 00:37:48.331
What's that?

511
00:37:49.734 --> 00:37:51.134
Settle an old score.

512
00:37:52.837 --> 00:37:54.032
The oldest score.

513
00:38:15.860 --> 00:38:17.089
Told ya.

514
00:38:49.727 --> 00:38:52.822
Look. Cass. I'm as glad as anyone
that Stella got her groove back. okay?

515
00:38:53.031 --> 00:38:54.727
But you let Metatron go?

516
00:38:55.066 --> 00:38:57.865
Dean. How many times are
you going to repeat that question?

517
00:38:58.102 --> 00:38:59.713
I'm gonna say it again!
You let Metatron go!

518
00:38:59.737 --> 00:39:01.365
He's not going anywhere.

519
00:39:01.573 --> 00:39:03.804
If he makes a move. if he
draws the slightest attention.

520
00:39:03.975 --> 00:39:05.855
the full force of angel-kind
will snuff him out.

521
00:39:06.344 --> 00:39:07.505
Look. you...

522
00:39:07.979 --> 00:39:10.107
Neither of you saw
him. He is a human.

523
00:39:10.481 --> 00:39:12.109
And a pitiable one at that.

524
00:39:12.417 --> 00:39:13.749
He's not a threat to us.

525
00:39:14.219 --> 00:39:16.552
Look. I mean. I
put him in traction.

526
00:39:16.754 --> 00:39:21.055
Guys. bigger fish to fry.
here. Amara is in the wind.

527
00:39:22.827 --> 00:39:24.386
Yeah. God's freaking sister.

528
00:39:25.697 --> 00:39:29.190
You said you were close.
Dean. How'd she get away?

529
00:39:30.335 --> 00:39:32.175
I'm sorry. what part of
"God's freaking sister"

530
00:39:32.203 --> 00:39:34.672
did you not understand? She
overpowered me. End of story.

531
00:39:40.111 --> 00:39:41.443
What's our plan. here. fellas?

532
00:39:41.646 --> 00:39:44.046
You said you got everything
you could out of Metatron. right?

533
00:39:44.549 --> 00:39:47.149
So. where on Earth are we gonna
find an answer on how to stop her?

534
00:39:50.154 --> 00:39:52.674
I don't suppose God's decided to
share any wisdom on the matter?

535
00:39:56.628 --> 00:39:58.062
I'll look into the lore.

536
00:42:20.405 --> 00:42:21.405
ENGLISH -SDH

